        "content": "{\"formal\": {\"statement\": \"open Set MvPolynomial in\\n∀ (T : ℝ)\\n(hT : T > 0), MeasureTheory.volume {t : ℝ | t ≥ T ∧ Nat.floor t = 2 * (Nat.floor (t - T))} = 1\", \"namespace\": \"\", \"supporting_declarations\": [], \"rendered\": \"∀ T > 0, ((MeasureTheory.volume {t | ((t ≥ T) ∧ (⌊t⌋₊ = (2 * ⌊(t - T)⌋₊)))}) = 1)\"}, \"signature\": \"(T : ℝ)\\n(hT : T > 0)\\n: MeasureTheory.volume {t : ℝ | t ≥ T ∧ Nat.floor t = 2 * (Nat.floor (t - T))} = 1\", \"informal\": \"If two cars travel around a track at constant speeds of one lap per hour, starting from the same point but at different times, prove that the total amount of time for which the first car has completed exactly twice as many laps as the second is exactly $1$ hour.\", \"docstring\": \"/--\\nIf two cars travel around a track at constant speeds of one lap per hour, starting from the same point but at different times, prove that the total amount of time for which the first car has completed exactly twice as many laps as the second is exactly $1$ hour.\\n-/\", \"prechecks\": {\"status\": \"completed\", \"hints\": [{\"kind\": \"natural_arithmetic_review\", \"status\": \"advisory\"}], \"vacuity\": \"unresolved\"}, \"advisory\": {\"paraphrase_status\": \"completed\", \"differences\": [\"Context\", \"Variables\", \"Mathematical operations\", \"Problem framing\"], \"paraphrase\": \"For all positive real numbers T, the volume of the set of real numbers t where t is greater than or equal to T and the floor of t equals twice the floor of (t minus T) is equal to 1.\", \"comparison_status\": \"completed\"}}"
